35,2,1,talk,Minato,,I found that only two firms are tendering. They are worried about the clay.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,May,,The fund only pays for planting and water. It does not cover paving or buildings.,"{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"The trees on the avenue died because no one watered them. The basin is still fine, though.","{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Victoria,,We have only seven staff left. But there are two volunteer groups helping out.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shunichi,,People walk on hard ground to the tram. The drainage calls have doubled since the cap.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Minato,,"@May, that fund restriction is tricky. It means we can't build much.","{""words"":12,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,May,,"@Minato, exactly. And the upkeep for planted ground is triple the cost of hard surfaces.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Minato""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Victoria, the volunteers are good, but they can't replace the missing staff for daily care.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[""Victoria""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Victoria,,"@Shizue, I know. But the specialist care is bought in. It is a patchwork.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shunichi,,"@May, if the upkeep is triple, we can't afford a big garden. The heat is also a problem.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""May""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Minato,,"The phasing notes say we can hoard the south, but not the center. That limits us.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,May,,"So, a plan with lots of water and plants will be very expensive to keep.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"A paved square might be cheaper to maintain, but it won't look like a park.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Victoria,,"If we choose something that needs constant attention, we will fail. We don't have the people.","{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shunichi,,"The data says people want open, firm ground. A wetland might not fit their needs.","{""words"":15,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Minato,,I am leaning towards something simple. The ground is risky for big earthworks.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,May,,I agree. We need to be careful with the budget. The long-term cost is the killer.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Shizue,,I think we should look at what has worked before. The basin worked. The trees didn't.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Victoria,,I am worried about the staffing. We need a plan that doesn't require a full team.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shunichi,,Let us see the candidates. I think the data points to a specific direction.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
